# Halen Morick — forest T2 basic duelist (knight, exile-hunter)

[title Halen Morick]
[image monsters/forest_knight.png]
[stats hp=18]

* move Attack
  narration: He steps in with a quick thrust, blade tracking your guard.
  narration: He shifts his weight and stabs for the gap above your hip.

* move Defend
  narration: He settles his stance, blade angled across his body.

* move Recover
  narration: He gives ground a half-step and resets his guard.

* move Heavy Slow Attack
  narration: Halen brings the sword down in a committed two-handed cut.

* move Heavy Power Defend
  narration: He raises the blade into a high hanging guard, both hands locked.

* intro
You see a man in heavy imperial plate walking down the road toward you.
Fine gear, not the rusted cast-offs you've seen in the nearby garrisons.
He halts some ten paces away and you do the same. "Didn't think I'd find
you walking the road, but here you are. You've left a fair few bodies in
your wake." He does a slight bow. "Halen Morick. I'm the one they've sent
to put you down." He draws his blade. "Take a moment. When you're ready,
we'll begin."

* win
+give_gold 10
+add_tag killed_halen_morick
Halen goes down with the same composure he came on with. He tries to say
something, and does not. You take a moment yourself, then keep walking.
Whoever sent him might send another, but not today.

* lose
Your legs give out and your weapon slips from your grasp. Somewhere, far
away, Halen is telling you that you fought well, good form. A bit slow on
the reverse, but the voice fades to silence.
